  icon: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 9266273b8f123004195741f969177dda, type: 3}
  title: Script folders
  sections:
  - heading: Game systems
    text: Game systems are anything directly related to cooking carnage (clients,
      ingredients, workstations, or anything dependent on cooking carnage's architecture)
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: Standalone systems
    text: Standalone systems are systems that can exist outside of cooking carnage.
      For exemple, CSV parsers, links with the google API, toolkits, etc. They should
      be defined in their own assembly definition. Standalone systems are very similar
      to packages, but are stored here if they were writtent by our dev team instead
      of coming from an external source.
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: Editor
    text: Any scripts that should live inside the editor only (Attributes, PropertyDrawers,
      CustomEditors, etc.)
    linkText: 
    url: 
  loadedLayout: 1
